translation:
Levha, {''}mucize kesim{''}
yaptıklarını söylüyor.
Bu nasıl bir stil acaba?

O kadar narin ama bir o
kadar cesur bir dokunuş;
izleyeni büyülüyor.

Asfaltlanmamış ama,
bakimi çok iyi yapılmış;
yürümesi kolay bir cadde.

Maskeler hiçbir zaman iki ayrı şey değildi;
aslında bir ve aynıydılar. Başından
beri birlikte olmaları gerekiyordu.

Henry açıkça bir şey saklıyor;
bunu anlatamıyor ya da anlatmak
istemiyor. Sırrı ne olabilir?

original:
This little girl has lost her mummy.
{''}Me mam has red hair. Oh aye, and she has
a pink handbag with a bear on it!{''}

There's a group of people talking nearby.
A: {''}Look how stylish everyone is today!{''}
B: {''}Hold on. This handbag isn't mine!{''}
C: {''}Hey! I may dress girly, but I'm a man!{''}
D: {''}My handbag is a blue one.{''}
E: {''}Hmm, this isn't my bag. It's got the
wrong pattern.{''}

Who is the girl's mum? Choose from A to E.

The prospective tenants of this row of
houses have some unusual requirements.
① {''}I want to live next to a red house!{''}
② {''}No blue neighbours, please. Oh, and a
house on the end is out of the question!{''}
③ {''}Two doors down from a yellow house,
and no neighbours the same colour as us!{''}
④ {''}I'm fine with any colour as long as it's
not blue or red!{''}

Can you repaint just one house so that
every tenant can have their dream home?
Touch a house to change its colour.

Four golfers named Mr Black, Mr White,
Mr Brown and Mr Blue were competing in a
tournament. The caddy didn't know who was
who, so she asked three of the four. One of
them, Mr Brown, told her a lie.

A: {''}B is Mr Black.{''}
B: {''}I'm not Mr Blue!{''}
C: {''}Mr White? That's D.{''}

So who is Mr Blue?

Ms A is complaining about the seat she had
for last night's play. Can you work out where
she was sitting?
① {''}The five of us sat in a row, with me in the
middle. Talk about a fifth wheel!{''}
② {''}Of course, I got stuck behind some oaf in
a top hat. I could hardly see the stage!{''}
③ {''}There were four seats between me and
the aisle to my right. I needed the loo,
but I didn't dare make a fuss!{''}
④ {''}Since my view was blocked, I took to
looking at my ticket and noticed the seat
number and row number were two apart.{''}

Four people are talking at the end of a
very enjoyable evening party. Comparing
watches, they realise that none of them
have the correct time.

A: {''}My watch is always 20 minutes slow!{''}
B: {''}This old thing is 10 minutes slow.{''}
C: {''}I set mine 5 minutes fast!{''}
D: {''}Mine is 10 minutes fast.{''}

What time is it?

A, B, C, D and E run a baker's, a patisserie,
a bookshop, a grocer's and a caf{'e}. Which
person runs which business?

A: {''}C and I both work close to the baker's
and the patisserie.{''}
B: {''}C and I haven't dropped by the caf{'e} for
ages!{''}
C: {''}D and I never bake bread. Neither A
nor B run the bookshop.{''}
D: {''}E and I often visit the caf{'e} and the
grocer's.{''}
E: {''}C and I both work near the grocer's.{''}

One day, four people took part in a racing
tournament. First, they held races of two,
then the winners raced against each other,
while the losers battled for third.

Can you work out the order based on the
comments below?

A: {''}I won one race and lost another.{''}
B: {''}I didn't make it to the final!{''}
C: {''}I'm just glad I beat A.{''}
D: {''}If only I hadn't lost to B...{''}

translation:
Bir gün, dört kişi bir yarış turnuvasına
katıldı. Önce ikişer kişilik yarışlar yapıldı;
sonra kazananlar birbirleriyle yarıştı,
kaybedenler ise üçüncülük için mücadele etti.

Aşağıdaki yorumlara bakarak
sıralamayı çıkarabilir misin?

A: {''}Bir yarışı kazandım, birini
kaybettim.{''} B: {''}Finale çıkamadım!{''}
C: {''}A'yı yenmiş olmama sevindim.{''}
D: {''}Keşke B'ye kaybetmeseydim...{''}

original:
Six people are talking at the casino.
A: {''}I've got a quarter of the chips I started
with!{''}
C: {''}If you add up the number of chips that B
and F lost, you'll get the amount that I had
to begin with.{''}
E: {''}I had the same number of chips as B did
at first, but now I've got more left.{''}
D: {''}I'm completely out of chips!{''}

Draw lines from the people (A to F) to the
stacks of chips (1 to 6) to identify which
chips belong to which person.

translation:
Sakinleşince yavru sincap, Tavşan'a
nerede oturduğunu söyledi;
Tavşan da onu annesine götürdü.

Karnaval arifesiydi;
ormanın tüm hayvanları
kutlamak için toplanmıştı.

original:
{''}But I also fancy a house like Squirrel's,
on a treetop, in the dappled sunshine,{''}
he reflected.

{''}Then again, a big, wide cave like Bear's
would be convenient, too - I could
invite everyone over at once!{''}

translation:
{''}Öte yandan, Bear'inki gibi büyük,
geniş bir mağara da işe yarar -
herkesi aynı anda davet edebilirdim!{''}

original:
{''}All our friends in the woods have
homes that are nice in different ways,
but I will always like my home best.{''}

translation:
{''}Ormandaki tüm dostlarımızın evleri
farklı şekillerde güzel, ama ben her
zaman kendi evimi en çok severim.{''}

Sonra sadece on patileri üzerinde
yürüdü! Müthiş bir güç gösterisiydi;
ama heyecanı onu biraz dengesiz yaptı.

Çocuğun hastalığı ağırlaştı;
Bunny'yi görmek için
pencereye bile gidemedi.
